    I am going to be teaching a 7-week course in Forth next Fall
 at Goucher College using F-PC.  The students will all have
 completed a 7-week course in FORTRAN.  Is there a book you
 would recommend for the class?   I need to choose a book soon.
    I have taught Forth twice before.  Once, I used MVP Forth
 with Starting Forth (1st ed.), then I used F83 with Mastering
 Forth.
    I was thinking of using either Mastering Forth, or Starting
 Forth (2nd ed.), but I'm open to other ideas (like Kelly &
 Spies).
    I understand you teach Forth using F-PC.  What book do you
 use?  Did you require students to also purchase a copy of
 Ting's System Guide to F-PC?  How did you work the cost of the
 program (did you get a site license from Tom Zimmer, or buy
 enough copies for the machines at your school, or what)?
    Thanks for the advice.

